id=a52sxq_shade_locked_collapse
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: no wallpaper-only gap when the shade is closed on the lock screen
author=kusti420
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE. Closing the notification shade / quick panel that was pulled down on the lock screen (status bar state SHADE_LOCKED) by a swipe ran NotificationPanelViewController.flingToHeight with the closing FlingAnimationUtils (secure lock + tracking): a velocity-matched curve capped at 0.6 s x sqrt(distance/height) whose long slow-in tail is spent below expansion 0.5, where One UI has already faded the quick panel content out (alpha = 2 x fraction - 1) and the window blur nearly to zero, while the clock, date, shortcuts and lock-screen status bar stay GONE until the fling ends and makeExpandedInvisible -> setState(KEYGUARD) re-expands the keyguard. Tester log 2026-10-16: 574 ms fling, 390 ms of it after the panel content reached alpha 0, plus 124 ms until the first keyguard frame = about 0.5 s of bare wallpaper (60 fps tester video: 15+ frames). For SHADE_LOCKED swipe collapses only, the fling is now linear at the finger's speed (1000 x height / |velocity| ms, clamped 150-300 ms), so the bare-wallpaper part shrinks to roughly half of a <= 300 ms collapse. Tap/back/command collapses (velocity 0, already the short accelerated 200-300 ms curve), the unlocked shade and the lock-screen swipe-up are unchanged.
